1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,890
A spear in one mantis shrimp.

2
00:00:02,240 --> 00:00:03,410
A hammer in another.

3
00:00:04,080 --> 00:00:07,090
At first, the difference was not so dramatic.

4
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:11,650
Early mantis shrimps had several pairs of
hunting limbs that looked broadly alike.

5
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:15,650
Over time, the front pair began
to stand apart from the others.

6
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:20,370
Across different lineages, that front
pair took two very different shapes.

7
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:25,410
In spearers, it developed a slender, spined
end for catching and piercing.

8
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:30,450
In smashers, its striking end became a compact,
thickened club, built to deliver

9
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:32,130
a powerful blow.

10
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:36,130
As the front pair changed, it stopped
being just another pair of limbs.

11
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:40,850
It became the animal's defining weapon
— a spear here, a hammer there.

12
00:00:41,360 --> 00:00:44,167
And that is how one shared hunting limb became:
